[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: 10 System requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: bench.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Level 1: what the vehicle as a whole shall do, independent of how it is split into functions and nodes. Verified by system tests on the bench. IDs: SYS-<AREA>-NNN. Each traces to a stakeholder need (STK).
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Exterior lighting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-LIGHT-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Direction indication
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle shall provide left and right direction indication on request.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-LIGHT-002
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
RELEVANCE: Safety
TITLE: Hazard warning
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle shall provide a hazard warning signal on request, which takes priority over direction indication.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-LIGHT-003
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Comfort blink
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle shall provide comfort blink: a short direction request produces a configured number of indication flashes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Lane-change convenience offered by most production vehicles; the number of flashes is market-specific and therefore configurable (variant coding).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-LIGHT-004
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Low beam
STATEMENT: >>>
The vehicle shall switch its low beam on and off on request.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Robustness and safe behaviour

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SAFE-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
RELEVANCE: Safety
TITLE: Defined degraded lighting state
STATEMENT: >>>
If a lighting node loses its commands, the vehicle shall enter a defined degraded lighting state that keeps the vehicle visible, and shall report that it is degraded.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-SAFE-002
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Non-functional
VERIFICATION: Analysis
MILESTONE: M1
RELEVANCE: Safety
TITLE: Deterministic node behaviour
STATEMENT: >>>
Every vehicle node shall behave deterministically and repeatably during start-up and normal operation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Diagnostics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-DIAG-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M3
TITLE: Diagnostic access to every node
STATEMENT: >>>
Every vehicle node shall provide its status and detected faults through a diagnostic interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-ARCH-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Constraint
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Functions decoupled from hardware
STATEMENT: >>>
Vehicle functions shall be decoupled from the hardware they run on, so that a hardware node can be replaced by its virtual twin without changing the functions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STK-005

[[/SECTION]]
